    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (74.97) and **Junior Caminero** (74.72) anchoring the lineup, both benefiting from highly favorable individual matchups. **Yordan Alvarez** faces Avila in a setup that maximizes his elite 0.452 xwOBA, while **Junior Caminero** exploits a generous 5.47 xERA from Aldegheri; the latter\u2019s ability to drive the ball against a weak lefty matchup makes him our premier utility play. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (73.03) rounds out the top tier, as his speed profile and the dynamic platoon advantage against Roupp solidify his position as a high-upside lead-off catalyst. We are heavily overweighting speed today, and with **Caleb Durbin** (60.06) facing a pitcher with a slow delivery, we anticipate a green light on the basepaths to help us close the gap in the scarce SB category.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Colt Keith** (56.96). While he narrowly missed the starting cut, his profile against Bibee was respectable, yet he was ultimately squeezed out by the consistency of **Casey Schmitt** (63.03) and the superior platoon dynamics afforded to **Luke Raley** (62.96). Managers should note the significant risk surrounding our middle-infield/outfield core: both **Trea Turner** (50.39) and **Kyle Schwarber** (49.63) are facing the formidable Misiorowski. With a 2.79 xERA, Misiorowski is an elite arm who drags down the efficiency scores for both players significantly, and we are monitoring these spots closely for potential cap management if they struggle through their first two at-bats. Conversely, we expect a bounce-back from **Christian Yelich** (47.61) despite the negative platoon weight, as his lead-off role remains a critical component of our offensive architecture.",
